A row flex container measured for its max-content size summed its items' flex base sizes, so flex: 1 items (a
zero basis) collapsed a shrink-to-fit toolbar to nothing. It now sums their max-content contributions (CSS
Flexbox 9.9.1, 9.9.3): each item's max-content width, bounded by a length flex basis where it cannot grow or
cannot shrink (a percentage basis is indefinite there), then by its min/max widths.

